{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-95514",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{|{e}^{x}|\\sqrt{1+{({e}^{x})}^{2}}})\\cdot ({e}^{x})^{′} \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{{e}^{x}\\cdot \\sqrt{1+{e}^{2x}}}\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1+{e}^{2x}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
